classDiagram
    direction LR

    class Person {
        +UUID personId
        +String documentType
        +String documentNumber
        +String name
        +String lastName
        +String email
        +String phone
        +String bloodType
        +Date birthDate
        +Boolean status
        +activate()
        +deactivate()
    }

    class AppUser {
        +UUID userId
        +UUID personId
        +String username
        +String passwordHash
        +AuthenticationType authenticationType
        +Boolean status
        +DateTime lastAccess
        +authenticate(credentials) UserSession
        +activate()
        +deactivate()
    }

    class UserSession {
        +UUID sessionId
        +UUID userId
        +DateTime startDate
        +DateTime endDate
        +String sourceIp
        +SessionStatus sessionStatus
        +close()
        +refresh() UserSession
    }

    class PasswordPolicy {
        +Int policyId
        +Int minLength
        +Int maxLength
        +Boolean requiresUppercase
        +Boolean requiresNumbers
        +Boolean requiresSymbols
        +Int expirationDays
    }

    class Role {
        +Int roleId
        +String roleName
        +String description
    }

    class Permission {
        +Int permissionId
        +String permissionName
        +String description
    }

    class RolePermission {
        +Int roleId
        +Int permissionId
        +DateTime assignmentDate
    }

    class UserRole {
        +UUID userId
        +Int roleId
        +DateTime assignmentDate
    }

    class Credentials {
        <<value object>>
        +String identifier
        +String password
    }

    class AuthenticationType {
        <<enumeration>>
        Local
        Windows
        External
    }

    class SessionStatus {
        <<enumeration>>
        Active
        Closed
    }

    Person "1" --> "0..1" AppUser : app_user.person_id FK, UNIQUE
    AppUser "1" --> "0..*" UserSession : user_session.user_id FK
    Role "1" --> "0..*" RolePermission : role_permission.role_id FK
    Permission "1" --> "0..*" RolePermission : role_permission.permission_id FK
    Role "1" --> "0..*" UserRole : user_role.role_id FK
    AppUser "1" ..> "0..*" UserRole : user_role.user_id — cross-context, no FK
    AppUser ..> Credentials : authenticate() consumes
    AppUser --> AuthenticationType
    UserSession --> SessionStatus

    note for Person "RN-01/RN-02: a Person may exist without an active AppUser, but an AppUser cannot exist without a Person. RN-03: cannot be deleted with active records. No school_id — identity is school-agnostic."
    note for AppUser "RN-04/RN-06: must authenticate before use; admins may deactivate without deleting history. person_id is UNIQUE — one account per person."
    note for UserSession "sessionId is the opaque bearer token (never a JWT). refresh() rotates it: closes this row and returns a new UserSession — single use."
    note for Role "RN-07: roles are global, no school_id. Seeds: Administrador, Instructor, Aprendiz (legacy SUPER_ADMIN/SCHOOL_ADMIN/INSTRUCTOR/STUDENT merged)."
    note for Permission "Format context.resource:action, e.g. attendance.justification:approve. RN-09/RN-10: access depends on the assigned role's permissions."
    note for UserRole "PK (user_id, role_id). RN-07: every AppUser must have at least one role."
    note "All classes also carry the standard audit block (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and `06-data/domains/01-identity.md` / `02-authorization.md` for the column-level ER view."
